%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
title: b1.1 What residents and staff value
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** Eight values, held by the stakeholders in a2.1. Social connectedness leads: residents want company and, over time, friends. Autonomy and privacy set its limits, because each resident decides whom to meet and what others may know about them. Dignity means that a forgotten name is never exposed. Truthfulness rules out deception, kind lies included, and leaves painful truths to a trusted person.

= Human Value - Autonomy [HV-01] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-01
|Name|Autonomy
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Each resident decides whom to meet, when, and what to do together. They choose what others may know about them, and can change their mind. Consent comes before every introduction and every shared fact.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02 (high); ST-05 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also supports Dignity.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: the resident sets and changes their own settings; a "no" ends the offer, and nobody asks why.

Violated: introductions arranged for staff convenience; a shared fact used without asking; persuasion; reminders of declined offers.
)))
|Source|Ryan, R. M. & Deci, E. L. (2000). Self-determination theory and the facilitation of intrinsic motivation, social development, and well-being. //American Psychologist//, 55(1), 68-78.

= Human Value - Dignity [HV-02] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-02
|Name|Dignity
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Residents are spoken to as adults. A forgotten name or fact passes without comment, and nobody is quizzed, corrected or praised for the obvious. Company is offered for the resident's sake, never to fill a timetable.
|Held by|ST-01 (high); ST-02 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: names given as a statement ("This is Jan"), so that nobody has to admit forgetting; slips pass without remark.

Violated: "You've met before, don't you remember?"; "You told me that already"; finishing someone's sentence; being paired off to fill an activity.
)))
|Source|Kitwood, T. (1997). //Dementia Reconsidered: The Person Comes First//. Open University Press. Goffman, E. (1967). //Interaction Ritual//. Anchor Books.

= Human Value - Privacy [HV-03] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-03
|Name|Privacy
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|(((
Each resident owns their life story, their secrets and their time alone. Nothing about one resident reaches another without consent, and the System's data stays in the care home.

Staff: their own work is not monitored.
)))
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02, ST-05, ST-07 (high); ST-04, ST-06 (medium); ST-03 (low - may want more shared than the resident would)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also supports Dignity.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: only consented facts are used to match or introduce; nothing leaves the home; time in one's room is noticed only where the resident agreed.

Violated: a secret told to the wrong person; a match explained by a fact its owner never released; a resident watched in their room.
)))
|Source|Friedman, B., Kahn, P. H., Jr. & Borning, A. (2008). Value Sensitive Design and Information Systems. In K. E. Himma & H. T. Tavani (Eds.), //The Handbook of Information and Computer Ethics//. Wiley. Niemeijer et al. (2010).

= Human Value - Safety [HV-04] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-04
|Name|Safety
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|No falls and no getting lost, also when residents spend time together. A walk in the garden needs walking assessed first and a member of staff at the door.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-04, ST-06, ST-07 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Instrumental: a condition for going out at all.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: walks together suggested only to residents assessed fit; incidents reach a person quickly.

Violated: a walk suggested to someone not assessed; a fall that nobody notices.
)))
|Source|Härlein, J. et al. (2009). Fall risk factors in older people with dementia or cognitive impairment. //Journal of Advanced Nursing//, 65(5), 922-933.

= Human Value - Well-being [HV-05] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-05
|Name|Well-being
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Calm, movement, fresh air, and days with something to look forward to. Emotional safety: no embarrassment, pressure or conflict, and no painful news at the wrong moment.
|Held by|ST-01 to ST-06 (high); ST-07 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: pleasure in time spent together; calm afterwards.

Violated: distress after an awkward introduction, a refusal made in public or a blunt answer.
)))
|Source|Forbes, D. et al. (2015). Exercise programs for people with dementia. //Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews//, (4), CD006489. Bratman et al. (2015).

= Human Value - Social connectedness [HV-06] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-06
|Name|Social connectedness
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Residents have company and conversation with each other and, over time, a friend. They feel less lonely.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-02, ST-03, ST-05 (high); ST-04 (medium)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Both. Valued in itself; also a reason to leave the room.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: introductions lead to further meetings; residents can name someone here they like to talk to.

Violated: the System in place of people; introductions that lead nowhere; withdrawal after an awkward meeting.
)))
|Source|Victor, C. R. (2012). Loneliness in care homes: a neglected area of research? //Aging Health//, 8(6), 637-646. Holwerda et al. (2014). de Medeiros et al. (2012).

= Human Value - Identity [HV-07] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-07
|Name|Identity
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|Residents remain who they were: their trade, places, people, interests and own words. A shared past gives two residents something to talk about.
|Held by|ST-01, ST-03, ST-05 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also gives conversation a subject.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: introductions built on the residents' own lives, in their own words.

Violated: wrong facts about a resident's life; a match made on a label, such as a diagnosis, rather than on a life.
)))
|Source|Kitwood (1997). Woods, B. et al. (2018). Reminiscence therapy for dementia. //Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews//, (3), CD001120.

= Human Value - Truthfulness [HV-08] =

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|HV-08
|Name|Truthfulness
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Provisional. Literature and group reasoning only.
|Situated meaning|(((
No deception by design: no lies, kind ones included, no denials, and no playing along with an untrue belief. Trust once lost is rarely regained.

Errors cannot be ruled out: a profile can be out of date, and the System can mishear an answer. So it states facts only from checked sources, says less when unsure, and corrects itself plainly when contradicted.

Painful truths (why the resident lives here, a death, a diagnosis) come from a trusted person, never from the System.
)))
|Held by|ST-01, ST-03, ST-04, ST-06 (high)
|Intrinsic or instrumental|Intrinsic. Also instrumental: trust is the condition for accepting any help.
|Recognition criteria|(((
Served: no untruth, denial or playing along in the script; errors corrected at once and fixed at their source; sensitive questions passed to the trusted person.

Violated: "You're only here for a few days"; an error left standing; the System states a death.
)))
|Source|Mental Health Foundation (2016). //What Is Truth?// James et al. (2006).

